"properties":{"cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.35.0","Node name for S&R":"CreateVideo"},"widgets_values":[30,"auto","sRGB"],"widgets_values_named":{"fps":30,"bit_depth":"auto","color_space":"sRGB"}},{"id":13,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-930,3760],"size":[387.03125,463.640625],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["# About SeedVR2 Video Upscale\n\n## How Resolution Works\n\nThe **Resolution** setting in the `SeedVR2_VideoUpscaler` node is based on the **height** of your output video. Think of it the same way you'd refer to standard video resolutions:\n\n| Resolution Setting | Output Example (16:9) |\n|----|-----|\n| 1080 | 1920×1080 (1080p) |\n| 1440 | 2560×1440 (1440p) |\n| 2160 | 3840×2160 (4K) |\n\nSo if your source is 1280×720 and you set Resolution to `1080`, the output will be **1920×1080**.\n\n## Preparing Your Input\n\nUse the **Image Scale** node before the upscaler to downscale your input to the correct starting size. The upscaler node will **center-crop** the input to ensure the final output lands on the correct aspect ratio, so getting your input dimensions right beforehand avoids unexpected cropping.\n\n## Performance Note\n\nHigher target resolutions require significantly more processing time. If you're experimenting or iterating, start at a lower resolution to dial in your settings before committing to a full 2160p render."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"# About SeedVR2 Video Upscale\n\n## How Resolution Works\n\nThe **Resolution** setting in the `SeedVR2_VideoUpscaler` node is based on the **height** of your output video. Think of it the same way you'd refer to standard video resolutions:\n\n| Resolution Setting | Output Example (16:9) |\n|----|-----|\n| 1080 | 1920×1080 (1080p) |\n| 1440 | 2560×1440 (1440p) |\n| 2160 | 3840×2160 (4K) |\n\nSo if your source is 1280×720 and you set Resolution to `1080`, the output will be **1920×1080**.\n\n## Preparing Your Input\n\nUse the **Image Scale** node before the upscaler to downscale your input to the correct starting size. The upscaler node will **center-crop** the input to ensure the final output lands on the correct aspect ratio, so getting your input dimensions right beforehand avoids unexpected cropping.\n\n## Performance Note\n\nHigher target resolutions require significantly more processing time. If you're experimenting or iterating, start at a lower resolution to dial in your settings before committing to a full 2160p render."},"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":22,"type":"ImageFromBatch","pos":[-60,3940],"size":[270,90],"flags":{},"order":4,"mode":4,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"图像","name":"image","type":"IMAGE","link":28},{"localized_name":"批次索引","name":"batch_index","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"batch_index"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"长度","name":"length","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"length"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"图像","name":"IMAGE","type":"IMAGE","links":[29]}],"properties":{"cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.35.0","Node name for S&R":"ImageFromBatch"},"widgets_values":[0,96],"widgets_values_named":{"batch_index":0,"length":96}},{"id":15,"type":"3531d186-daf3-492a-bb11-94a4c791a3f3","pos":[230,3760],"size":[333,114],"flags":{},"order":6,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"image","name":"image","type":"IMAGE","link":27},{"name":"resolution","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"resolution"},"link":null},{"name":"model","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"model"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"IMAGE","name":"IMAGE","type":"IMAGE","links":[24]}],"properties":{"cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.35.0","proxyWidgetErrorQuarantine":[{"originalEntry":["-1","resolution"],"reason":"missingSourceNode","hostValue":1080,"attemptedAtVersion":1},{"originalEntry":["-1","model"],"reason":"missingSourceNode","hostValue":"seedvr2_ema_7b_fp16.safetensors","attemptedAtVersion":1},{"originalEntry":["4","seed"],"reason":"missingSourceWidget","attemptedAtVersion":1}],"previewExposures":[]},"widgets_va